<!--
    v1.13.0 demo — report intelligence.

    This definition exercises the v1.13.0 territory (ROADMAP v1.13.0) in one
    report: the Report dependencies scope draws the report → dataset → object
    → column chain built on the v1.9.0 catalogue and the v1.11.0 column
    contract.

    What to observe in the app after Apply in the Reports menu, then switch
    Scope to "Report dependencies":

      1. The report node links to each dataset (embedded, shared, unresolved).
      2. Each embedded dataset links to the objects its query reads/writes/
         calls, and each object links to the columns its query references.
      3. The Filter report menu hides datasets by kind, the column layer, or
         external objects — presentation only, never changing the graph.
      4. The report graph exports to Mermaid and draw.io with provenance
         metadata on its documented `report` layout class.

    The embedded dataset queries are plain T-SQL, so they also analyse cleanly
    as query structure when selected from the Dataset picker:

       SELECT StudentId, StudentName FROM dbo.Student WHERE SchoolYear = @Year
       SELECT CourseId, CourseName FROM dbo.Course

    To resolve dbo.* objects to their canonical identity and verify the
    object→column layer by catalogue evidence, paste this catalogue in the
    Catalogue menu and Apply, then re-run:

       dbo.Student TABLE student
       dbo.Course TABLE
       COL dbo.Student.StudentId
       COL dbo.Student.StudentName
       COL dbo.Student.SchoolYear
       COL dbo.Course.CourseId
       COL dbo.Course.CourseName

    Large-graph report layout convergence remains scheduled for v1.14.0.

    This demo is an illustration, not an input to the fixture-corpus metrics
    (docs/metrics-v1.13.0.json). No user input or runtime telemetry is
    collected.
-->
<Report xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/sqlserver/reporting/2008/01/reportdefinition" xmlns:rd="http://schemas.microsoft.com/SQLServer/reporting/reportdesigner">
  <DataSources>
    <DataSource Name="SchoolDB">
      <ConnectionProperties>
        <DataProvider>SQL</DataProvider>
        <ConnectString>Data Source=.;Initial Catalog=School;Integrated Security=true</ConnectString>
      </ConnectionProperties>
    </DataSource>
    <DataSource Name="SharedStore">
      <DataSourceReference>Shared/SharedStore</DataSourceReference>
    </DataSource>
  </DataSources>
  <DataSets>
    <DataSet Name="StudentMaster">
      <Query>
        <DataSourceName>SchoolDB</DataSourceName>
        <CommandText>SELECT StudentId, StudentName FROM dbo.Student WHERE SchoolYear = @Year</CommandText>
        <QueryParameters>
          <QueryParameter Name="Year">
            <Value>=Parameters!Year.Value</Value>
          </QueryParameter>
        </QueryParameters>
      </Query>
      <Fields>
        <Field Name="StudentId"><DataField>StudentId</DataField></Field>
        <Field Name="StudentName"><DataField>StudentName</DataField></Field>
      </Fields>
    </DataSet>
    <DataSet Name="CourseLookup">
      <Query>
        <DataSourceName>SchoolDB</DataSourceName>
        <CommandText>SELECT CourseId, CourseName FROM dbo.Course</CommandText>
      </Query>
    </DataSet>
    <DataSet Name="SharedRollup">
      <SharedDataSet>
        <SharedDataSetReference>Shared/Rollup</SharedDataSetReference>
      </SharedDataSet>
    </DataSet>
    <DataSet Name="Broken">
      <Query>
        <DataSourceName>SchoolDB</DataSourceName>
      </Query>
    </DataSet>
  </DataSets>
  <Body>
    <ReportItems>
      <Textbox Name="Header">
        <Value>= "Student directory"</Value>
      </Textbox>
      <Tablix Name="StudentTable">
        <TablixDataRegion>
          <DataSetName>StudentMaster</DataSetName>
        </TablixDataRegion>
      </Tablix>
    </ReportItems>
  </Body>
</Report>